    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. I'm wondering about the kinetic stability though. Even with that steric barrier, we're still seeing some minor coalescence over long-term storage. Is there a way the protonation of the headgroups might actually weaken that protective layer, or is it more likely an issue with the surfactant concentration not being high enough to fully cover the surface area?), specifically when the acidity fluctuates during the manufacturing process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
