      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Fluctuating pH can indeed destabilize the interfacial film by altering the charge density and hydration shell around lecithin. While high surface coverage is paramount, rapid $\\text{pH}$ swings can induce desorption or structural rearrangement in the protective layer, temporarily reducing the steric barrier. It's possible that the ionic strength changes accompanying $\\text{pH}$ shifts might also compress the electrical double layer, allowing droplets to approach more closely than intended by the surfactant alone.",
      "source": "target",
